      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Hello, docteh\n\nAbout the logs, I was unable to look at them because VRChat did not provide any information about the crash when it crashed, and to be honest i was lazy.  It wasn't just VRChat that crashed; the entire Unity game crashed without explanation.  I tried many things to fix the crashing issue, but none worked. It seems like VRChat may have faulty code that leads to a crash, but for some reason, this issue is not a problem when playing on desktop.\n\nBy the way, I tried restarting my PC and Oculus, changing the graphics settings and resolution, using wireless Oculus Link, OculusKill, updating my Nvidia drivers, and many other options. Out of frustration, I stopped playing VRChat for a while, except for occasional desktop mode use.\n\nAlso, I was in a private server when experimenting with the issue.\n\nSo, my only option was to use the GPT format, and i didnt want to because of my limited data on my phone\n\nI'm really hoping for a patch soon.\n\nAnd i hope this makes it a bit more clear on the issue im experiencing.",
